# uACPI's test cases this kernel does not pass, read by tools/acpi/uacpi_cases.py, one per line:
# <case> <why>, where <why> is the section of docs/acpi/specification.md that decides otherwise, or #<issue>
# for a case that waits for that issue. A listed case that passes fails the run, so that the list stays true.
bad-opcodes §1.4 out of scope: `Load` from a Buffer fails with load_form_unsupported, where the case loads its tables from Buffers
bogus-pci #58: its root bridge is in segment 0xDEAD, which needs ECAM and fails with address_unreachable until then, where uACPI reads all ones
indices-1 §5.2 mixed-type operands: Concatenate turns an Integer into 16 hexadecimal digits, as ACPICA does, where uACPI writes the shortest lowercase form
indices-2 §5.2 references: a reference to a local dies with its frame, where uACPI keeps the local alive
infinite-recursion §6.1 limits: 64 frames, the table's code included, stop the recursion at 63 calls, where the case wants more than 64
osi §5.4 the Windows identity: no runner string ("TestRunner", "AnotherTestString") answers True, and "Windows 2006" answers True and "Extended Address Space Descriptor" False, where the case wants the answers of uACPI's or acpiexec's own runner
package-reference-cycle §1.4 out of scope: `Load` from a Buffer fails with load_form_unsupported, where the case loads its tables from Buffers
read-fields-on-deref §6.2 errors: a region on physical page 0 is unreachable, the kernel mapping no window there
read-from-deleted-field §1.4 out of scope: a `LoadTable` that table-level code runs while its table is declared fails with load_form_unsupported, where the case's DSDT loads itself again
reference-cycle-via-reg §1.4 out of scope: `Load` from a Buffer fails with load_form_unsupported, where the case loads its tables from Buffers
reg-orphan-ec #547: the _REG of the EmbeddedControl space comes with the EC handler, for an EC that declares no region of it too
reg-vs-copy-object #547: the _REG of the EmbeddedControl space, and its disconnection, come with the EC handler
table-loading-0 §1.4 out of scope: `Load` from a Buffer fails with load_form_unsupported, where the case loads its tables from Buffers
table-loading-2 §1.4 out of scope: `Load` from a Buffer fails with load_form_unsupported, where the case loads its tables from Buffers
table-loading-3 §1.4 out of scope: `LoadTable` with a ParameterPath and ParameterData fails with load_form_unsupported
table-loading-4 §1.4 out of scope: `LoadTable` with a RootPath, a ParameterPath and ParameterData fails with load_form_unsupported
table-overrides §1.4 out of scope: `Load` from a Buffer fails with load_form_unsupported, where the case loads its tables from Buffers
